course: dictionary
lesson: 14532
title: A word that means for ever
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Perpetuity is a long, serious word. It means lasting for ever, with no end. You will mostly meet it in one phrase: «in perpetuity», which means for ever.
explain: Grown-ups use it in law, money and important papers. «The town was given the park in perpetuity.» The words around it tell you the gift has no end: the park belongs to the town for ever.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The town was given the park for ever.» It still makes sense, so you have found the meaning. Perpetuity is a formal word, so it is more likely to appear in a document or a serious story than in everyday chat.
fact: Perpetuity means lasting for ever or for an endless time.
fact: It is mostly used in the phrase «in perpetuity», which means for ever.
fact: In money, a perpetuity is a payment that goes on for ever.
fact: In law, papers may say a right or a piece of land is given «in perpetuity», so it can never end.
fact: Perpetuity is a noun, and it is usually heard in formal writing, not in everyday talk.
exercise: «The land was given to the village in perpetuity.» What does in perpetuity mean? | For one year, and then it is sold | For a single afternoon | Only on Sundays | *For ever
exercise: «The payment will go on in perpetuity, year after year.» What does this suggest? | The payment is paid only once | The payment is very small | *The payment keeps going with no end | The payment stops after one year
exercise: Ella guesses perpetuity is a type of pet. What does it really mean? | Quick and short | *Lasting for ever | Very small | A type of pet
test: «The wizard promised his spell would last in perpetuity.» What does this sentence tell you? | The spell was cast by a child | *The spell will never end | The wizard forgot the spell | The spell will end soon
test: Which swap keeps the meaning of «in perpetuity»? | For a short while | Now and then | *For ever | Sometimes
exam: «The old tree's protection was written to last in perpetuity.» What does in perpetuity mean? | Until someone forgets | *For ever | Only in winter | For a short time
